{"parentUuid":"1ab217f4-2e14-4c56-abc5-896d0b0bb638","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"ebc1ac48-ebfd-4ee7-8dcd-a3ea8d9b44df","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"nifty-snuggling-cocoa","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_vrtx_01Jh1aivwtW6mPtEZdAXNEBZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01WtSpbhtmmsDNqEeHeMGtQ5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/pandas-excel-handling.md","content":"# Pandas Excel File Handling\n\n## Overview\nPandas is a powerful Python library for data manipulation and analysis. It provides excellent support for reading and writing Excel files through the `openpyxl` and `xlrd` engines.\n\n## Installation\n```bash\npip install pandas openpyxl xlrd\n```\n\n## Reading Excel Files\n\n### Basic Reading\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Read an Excel file\ndf = pd.read_excel('data.xlsx')\n\n# Read specific sheet\ndf = pd.read_excel('data.xlsx', sheet_name='Sheet1')\n\n# Read all sheets\nall_sheets = pd.read_excel('data.xlsx', sheet_name=None)\n```\n\n### Common Parameters\n- `sheet_name`: Specify which sheet to read (default is 0 for first sheet)\n- `header`: Row number to use as column names (default is 0)\n- `usecols`: Columns to read (can be column names or indices)\n- `nrows`: Number of rows to read\n- `dtype`: Data type for data or columns\n\n### Example: Reading Large Files\n```python\n# Read only first 1000 rows\ndf = pd.read_excel('large_file.xlsx', nrows=1000)\n\n# Read specific columns\ndf = pd.read_excel('data.xlsx', usecols=['A', 'B', 'C'])\n```\n\n## Data Inspection\n\n```python\n# View first few rows\nprint(df.head())\n\n# View last few rows\nprint(df.tail())\n\n# Get DataFrame shape\nprint(df.shape)  # (rows, columns)\n\n# Get column names\nprint(df.columns)\n\n# Get data types\nprint(df.dtypes)\n\n# Get basic statistics\nprint(df.describe())\n\n# Get info about DataFrame\nprint(df.info())\n```\n\n## Data Access and Filtering\n\n```python\n# Access column\ncolumn_data = df['column_name']\n\n# Access multiple columns\nsubset = df[['col1', 'col2']]\n\n# Access rows by index\nrow = df.iloc[0]  # First row\nrows = df.iloc[0:10]  # First 10 rows\n\n# Filter rows by condition\nfiltered = df[df['column_name'] > 100]\n\n# Multiple conditions\nfiltered = df[(df['col1'] > 10) & (df['col2'] < 100)]\n```\n\n## Common Operations\n\n```python\n# Count values\ncount = df['column'].value_counts()\n\n# Group by and aggregate\ngrouped = df.groupby('category')['value'].sum()\n\n# Sort values\nsorted_df = df.sort_values('column_name', ascending=False)\n\n# Unique values\nunique_vals = df['column'].unique()\n\n# Missing values\nmissing = df.isnull().sum()\n```\n\n## Writing to Files\n\n```python\n# Write to Excel\ndf.to_excel('output.xlsx', index=False)\n\n# Write to CSV\ndf.to_csv('output.csv', index=False)\n\n# Write to text file\ndf.to_csv('output.txt', sep='\\t', index=False)\n```\n\n## Memory Optimization\n\nFor large files:\n```python\n# Use chunking for very large files\nchunks = pd.read_excel('large.xlsx', chunksize=10000)\nfor chunk in chunks:\n    process(chunk)\n\n# Specify dtypes to reduce memory\ndf = pd.read_excel('data.xlsx', dtype={'col1': 'int32', 'col2': 'float32'})\n```\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":132,"cache_read_input_tokens":43344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":132,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXbAkqhfhBDcV92S6nkaZ","type":"assistant","uuid":"1f2f9353-159a-4b64-88d7-dc52f26ee006","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:08:06.883Z"}
{"parentUuid":"1f2f9353-159a-4b64-88d7-dc52f26ee006","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"ebc1ac48-ebfd-4ee7-8dcd-a3ea8d9b44df","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"nifty-snuggling-cocoa","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_vrtx_01Jh1aivwtW6mPtEZdAXNEBZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01NQPm34xPNNYEmbTFrJcnZM","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/pdf-text-extraction.md","content":"# PDF Text Extraction with Python\n\n## Overview\nPython offers several libraries for extracting text from PDF files. The most common ones are PyPDF2, pdfplumber, and PyMuPDF (fitz).\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\n# PyPDF2 - Simple and lightweight\npip install PyPDF2\n\n# pdfplumber - Better for tables and complex layouts\npip install pdfplumber\n\n# PyMuPDF - Fast and feature-rich\npip install PyMuPDF\n```\n\n## Using PyPDF2\n\n```python\nimport PyPDF2\n\n# Open and read PDF\nwith open('document.pdf', 'rb') as file:\n    pdf_reader = PyPDF2.PdfReader(file)\n\n    # Get number of pages\n    num_pages = len(pdf_reader.pages)\n\n    # Extract text from all pages\n    text = ''\n    for page in pdf_reader.pages:\n        text += page.extract_text()\n\n    print(text)\n\n# Extract text from specific page\nwith open('document.pdf', 'rb') as file:\n    pdf_reader = PyPDF2.PdfReader(file)\n    first_page = pdf_reader.pages[0]\n    text = first_page.extract_text()\n```\n\n## Using pdfplumber\n\n```python\nimport pdfplumber\n\n# Read PDF\nwith pdfplumber.open('document.pdf') as pdf:\n    # Extract text from all pages\n    full_text = ''\n    for page in pdf.pages:\n        full_text += page.extract_text()\n\n    # Extract tables\n    first_page = pdf.pages[0]\n    tables = first_page.extract_tables()\n\n    # Get page dimensions\n    width = first_page.width\n    height = first_page.height\n```\n\n## Using PyMuPDF (fitz)\n\n```python\nimport fitz  # PyMuPDF\n\n# Open PDF\ndoc = fitz.open('document.pdf')\n\n# Extract text from all pages\ntext = ''\nfor page_num in range(len(doc)):\n    page = doc[page_num]\n    text += page.get_text()\n\n# Extract text from specific page\npage = doc[0]\ntext = page.get_text()\n\n# Close document\ndoc.close()\n\n# Alternative: Context manager\nwith fitz.open('document.pdf') as doc:\n    text = ''\n    for page in doc:\n        text += page.get_text()\n```\n\n## Handling Common Issues\n\n### Encrypted PDFs\n```python\nimport PyPDF2\n\nwith open('encrypted.pdf', 'rb') as file:\n    pdf_reader = PyPDF2.PdfReader(file)\n\n    if pdf_reader.is_encrypted:\n        pdf_reader.decrypt('password')\n\n    text = pdf_reader.pages[0].extract_text()\n```\n\n### Extracting Tables\n```python\nimport pdfplumber\nimport pandas as pd\n\nwith pdfplumber.open('document.pdf') as pdf:\n    page = pdf.pages[0]\n    tables = page.extract_tables()\n\n    # Convert to DataFrame\n    for table in tables:\n        df = pd.DataFrame(table[1:], columns=table[0])\n        print(df)\n```\n\n### Handling Multiple Languages\n```python\nimport fitz\n\ndoc = fitz.open('multilingual.pdf')\nfor page in doc:\n    # Extract text with layout preservation\n    text = page.get_text(\"text\")  # Plain text\n    # or\n    text = page.get_text(\"blocks\")  # Text blocks with coordinates\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Choose the right library**:\n   - PyPDF2: Simple text extraction\n   - pdfplumber: Tables and complex layouts\n   - PyMuPDF: Speed and features\n\n2. **Handle encoding issues**:\n   ```python\n   text = text.encode('utf-8', errors='ignore').decode('utf-8')\n   ```\n\n3. **Clean extracted text**:\n   ```python\n   import re\n   # Remove extra whitespace\n   text = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text).strip()\n   ```\n\n4. **Memory management for large PDFs**:\n   ```python\n   # Process page by page instead of loading all at once\n   with pdfplumber.open('large.pdf') as pdf:\n       for i, page in enumerate(pdf.pages):\n           text = page.extract_text()\n           process_text(text)  # Process immediately\n   ```\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":132,"cache_read_input_tokens":43344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":132,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXbAkqhfhBDcV92S6nkaZ","type":"assistant","uuid":"78ce6527-1797-4307-9a3c-d51347415682","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:08:20.716Z"}
{"parentUuid":"78ce6527-1797-4307-9a3c-d51347415682","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"ebc1ac48-ebfd-4ee7-8dcd-a3ea8d9b44df","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"nifty-snuggling-cocoa","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_vrtx_01Jh1aivwtW6mPtEZdAXNEBZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_017HpTGnukDdvoP4iwDyng2P","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/python-game-comparison.md","content":"# Game Comparison and Scoring Analysis\n\n## Overview\nThis skill covers techniques for comparing game results, determining winners, and analyzing match outcomes in competitive scenarios.\n\n## Basic Concepts\n\n### Match Winner Determination\nWhen comparing two players' game results:\n1. Higher score wins\n2. Lower score wins (golf-style)\n3. Specific outcome comparison (win/loss/draw)\n\n### Pairing Games\nWhen matching odd-numbered games against even-numbered games:\n- Game 1 vs Game 2 (Match 1)\n- Game 3 vs Game 4 (Match 2)\n- Game 5 vs Game 6 (Match 3)\n- etc.\n\n## Implementation Patterns\n\n### Example 1: Simple Score Comparison\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Assuming df has columns: game_number, score\ndf = pd.read_excel('games.xlsx')\n\n# Separate odd and even games\nodd_games = df[df['game_number'] % 2 == 1].reset_index(drop=True)\neven_games = df[df['game_number'] % 2 == 0].reset_index(drop=True)\n\n# Compare scores\nplayer1_wins = 0\nplayer2_wins = 0\n\nfor i in range(min(len(odd_games), len(even_games))):\n    if odd_games.loc[i, 'score'] > even_games.loc[i, 'score']:\n        player1_wins += 1\n    elif odd_games.loc[i, 'score'] < even_games.loc[i, 'score']:\n        player2_wins += 1\n    # If equal, it's a draw (not counted)\n\nresult = player1_wins - player2_wins\nprint(f\"Result: {result}\")\n```\n\n### Example 2: Using Vectorized Operations\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\ndf = pd.read_excel('games.xlsx')\n\n# Create separate DataFrames for odd and even games\nodd_games = df[df['game_number'] % 2 == 1].copy()\neven_games = df[df['game_number'] % 2 == 0].copy()\n\n# Reset indices for alignment\nodd_games = odd_games.reset_index(drop=True)\neven_games = even_games.reset_index(drop=True)\n\n# Vectorized comparison\nplayer1_wins = (odd_games['score'] > even_games['score']).sum()\nplayer2_wins = (odd_games['score'] < even_games['score']).sum()\n\nresult = player1_wins - player2_wins\n```\n\n### Example 3: Handling Different Data Structures\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# If data has Player1 and Player2 columns already\ndf = pd.read_excel('games.xlsx')\n\n# Direct comparison\ndf['winner'] = df.apply(\n    lambda row: 'Player1' if row['Player1_score'] > row['Player2_score']\n    else ('Player2' if row['Player1_score'] < row['Player2_score'] else 'Draw'),\n    axis=1\n)\n\nplayer1_wins = (df['winner'] == 'Player1').sum()\nplayer2_wins = (df['winner'] == 'Player2').sum()\nresult = player1_wins - player2_wins\n```\n\n### Example 4: Handling Missing or Unmatched Games\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndf = pd.read_excel('games.xlsx')\n\n# Separate by odd/even\nodd_games = df[df['game_number'] % 2 == 1].sort_values('game_number')\neven_games = df[df['game_number'] % 2 == 0].sort_values('game_number')\n\n# Only compare where both games exist\nmin_pairs = min(len(odd_games), len(even_games))\n\nodd_games = odd_games.head(min_pairs).reset_index(drop=True)\neven_games = even_games.head(min_pairs).reset_index(drop=True)\n\n# Compare\ncomparisons = odd_games['score'].values > even_games['score'].values\nplayer1_wins = comparisons.sum()\nplayer2_wins = (~comparisons).sum() - (odd_games['score'].values == even_games['score'].values).sum()\n\nresult = player1_wins - player2_wins\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Aggregating Results\n```python\n# Count wins by player\nwin_counts = {\n    'Player1': player1_wins,\n    'Player2': player2_wins,\n    'Draws': draws\n}\n\n# Calculate win percentage\ntotal_matches = player1_wins + player2_wins + draws\nplayer1_win_pct = player1_wins / total_matches if total_matches > 0 else 0\n```\n\n### Debugging Comparisons\n```python\n# Create a detailed comparison DataFrame\ncomparison_df = pd.DataFrame({\n    'Match': range(1, len(odd_games) + 1),\n    'Game1': odd_games['game_number'].values,\n    'Score1': odd_games['score'].values,\n    'Game2': even_games['game_number'].values,\n    'Score2': even_games['score'].values,\n    'Winner': ['Player1' if s1 > s2 else ('Player2' if s1 < s2 else 'Draw')\n               for s1, s2 in zip(odd_games['score'].values, even_games['score'].values)]\n})\n\nprint(comparison_df)\n```\n\n## Edge Cases to Consider\n\n1. **Odd number of total games**: Last game has no pair\n2. **Missing game numbers**: Gaps in sequence\n3. **Tied scores**: How to handle draws\n4. **Data quality**: Invalid scores, missing data\n5. **Game ordering**: Ensure correct pairing\n\n## Output Formatting\n\n```python\n# Write single number to file\nwith open('answer.txt', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(str(result))\n\n# Or with more context (if needed)\nwith open('answer.txt', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(f\"{result}\\n\")\n```\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":132,"cache_read_input_tokens":43344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":132,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXbAkqhfhBDcV92S6nkaZ","type":"assistant","uuid":"fd0cd2ab-12b4-4605-9c36-86088591aa86","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:08:42.107Z"}
