ing Vectorized Operations\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\ndf = pd.read_excel('games.xlsx')\n\n# Create separate DataFrames for odd and even games\nodd_games = df[df['game_number'] % 2 == 1].copy()\neven_games = df[df['game_number'] % 2 == 0].copy()\n\n# Reset indices for alignment\nodd_games = odd_games.reset_index(drop=True)\neven_games = even_games.reset_index(drop=True)\n\n# Vectorized comparison\nplayer1_wins = (odd_games['score'] > even_games['score']).sum()\nplayer2_wins = (odd_games['score'] < even_games['score']).sum()\n\nresult = player1_wins - player2_wins\n```\n\n### Example 3: Handling Different Data Structures\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# If data has Player1 and Player2 columns already\ndf = pd.read_excel('games.xlsx')\n\n# Direct comparison\ndf['winner'] = df.apply(\n    lambda row: 'Player1' if row['Player1_score'] > row['Player2_score']\n    else ('Player2' if row['Player1_score'] < row['Player2_score'] else 'Draw'),\n    axis=1\n)\n\nplayer1_wins = (df['winner'] == 'Player1').sum()\nplayer2_wins = (df['winner'] == 'Player2').sum()\nresult = player1_wins - player2_wins\n```\n\n### Example 4: Handling Missing or Unmatched Games\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndf = pd.read_excel('games.xlsx')\n\n# Separate by odd/even\nodd_games = df[df['game_number'] % 2 == 1].sort_values('game_number')\neven_games = df[df['game_number'] % 2 == 0].sort_values('game_number')\n\n# Only compare where both games exist\nmin_pairs = min(len(odd_games), len(even_games))\n\nodd_games = odd_games.head(min_pairs).reset_index(drop=True)\neven_games = even_games.head(min_pairs).reset_index(drop=True)\n\n# Compare\ncomparisons = odd_games['score'].values > even_games['score'].values\nplayer1_wins = comparisons.sum()\nplayer2_wins = (~comparisons).sum() - (odd_games['score'].values == even_games['score'].values).sum()\n\nresult = player1_wins - player2_wins\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Aggregating Results\n```python\n# Count wins by player\nwin_counts = {\n    'Player1': player1_wins,\n    'Player2': player2_wins,\n    'Draws': draws\n}\n\n# Calculate win percentage\ntotal_matches = player1_wins + player2_wins + draws\nplayer1_win_pct = player1_wins / total_matches if total_matches > 0 else 0\n```\n\n### Debugging Comparisons\n```python\n# Create a detailed comparison DataFrame\ncomparison_df = pd.DataFrame({\n    'Match': range(1, len(odd_games) + 1),\n    'Game1': odd_games['game_number'].values,\n    'Score1': odd_games['score'].values,\n    'Game2': even_games['game_number'].values,\n    'Score2': even_games['score'].values,\n    'Winner': ['Player1' if s1 > s2 else ('Player2' if s1 < s2 else 'Draw')\n               for s1, s2 in zip(odd_games['score'].values, even_games['score'].values)]\n})\n\nprint(comparison_df)\n```\n\n## Edge Cases to Consider\n\n1. **Odd number of total games**: Last game has no pair\n2. **Missing game numbers**: Gaps in sequence\n3. **Tied scores**: How to handle draws\n4. **Data quality**: Invalid scores, missing data\n5. **Game ordering**: Ensure correct pairing\n\n## Output Formatting\n\n```python\n# Write single number to file\nwith open('answer.txt', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(str(result))\n\n# Or with more context (if needed)\nwith open('answer.txt', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(f\"{result}\\n\")\n```\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fd0cd2ab-12b4-4605-9c36-86088591aa86"}
